{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>Remember the days of eternity.</b> He said four divisions, corresponding to four things that he said in the preceding verse. Corresponding to his saying ״הֲלֹא הוּא אָבִיךָ״, which alludes that He is the Creator, he said ״זְכֹר יְמוֹת עוֹלָם״ — these are the six days of Genesis; there one will find that He who forms is He who creates. And corresponding to his saying ״קָּנֶךָ״, which alludes to the exodus from Egypt and the rest of the kindnesses by which He acquired us, he said ״בִּינוּ שְׁנוֹת דּוֹר וָדוֹר״ — that one should contemplate what HaShem did in the years of two generations, which are the generation that came out of Egypt and the fourth generation that entered the land, and through them one will recognize His deeds, may He be blessed, toward Israel, by which ״קָנֶךָ״. And corresponding to his saying ״עָשְׂךָ״, which is the sup rectification that we explained there — that He placed His Shekhinah among us and prophesied to us — he said ״שְׁאַל אָבִיךָ וְיַגֵּדְךָ״: your father — these are the prophets, as our Rabbis of blessed memory interpreted it (Sifrei). And corresponding to ״וַיְכֹנְנֶךָ״, which we explained as the preparations of the World to Come, he said ״זְקֵנֶיךָ וְיֹאמְרוּ לָךְ״ — meaning, these are the sages of Israel who recognize the preparation of the thing and what is grasped of the World to Come; they will tell you."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:21:12.110726455Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}